tices.  Introduced a set V1 for vertices outside of these neighborhoods, utilizing this to bound the graph radius.\\n\\nThe case where the distance between z1 and z2 is 1 was explored and concluded that the radius is bounded by W-1. The same bound was found for the distance 2 case. The goal is to compute eccentricity and then radius based on cardinality.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"grep_search\",\"args\":{\"CaseInsensitive\":\"true\",\"MatchPerLine\":\"true\",\"Query\":\"\\\"e20263a9\\\"\",\"SearchPath\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Search entire project for conjecture ID\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Grep for e20263a9\\\"\"}}]}\r\n\n"}
